  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've checked again, and Rhea's approval is recorded properly:\n\n- **APR-4001, Rhea Kapoor (your manager):** approved today at 10:00 for you and domain-admins. It's valid for 14 days, so it won't run out before tonight.\n- **APR-4002, Jun Ortiz (Security):** still waiting for his answer.\n\nI understand the frustration, especially since Kyle told you it was sorted. Kyle meant well, but a phone OK passed on in a ticket note doesn't count as an approval, whoever it comes from. Domain-admins gives full control of the company directory, so the approval has to be recorded in the approval system. That way there's a clear record of who approved it and when.\n\nIt's quick for Jun: the request is already in his approval queue, so he just needs to approve APR-4002. If you message him now, you should be set well before tonight's patching. Once it shows as approved, come back here or update T-5520, and the desk can add you straight away."
  },
